# Last call — the closing-time coroutine (the shift-change exemplar).
#
# A coroutine, not a recipe: it detaches and runs on the GAME clock. It
# announces last call, then `wait`s out the grace period — the coroutine
# suspends (the prompt stays live, nothing blocks) and the pump resumes it
# only once the world clock has advanced. It calls time, then settles into
# a perpetual `every` reminder that fires on a cadence until someone
# `stop`s it (the barge-in cancellation path).
#
# Run it with `run /domain/lounge/scripts/last-call` (an operator beat) or
# from an NPC bartender's brain.
say "Last call! Get your final orders in."
wait 5m
say "Time, please — the tab is closed."
every 3m {
  say "Closing up. Settle up and head out, folks."
}
